  "body": "## What changed\n\n**The report**: analytics export \"exports nothing or just a few sloppy rows\".\n\n**Root cause (two real bugs, shipped since 5.2.0):**\n1. **CSV and XLSX detail exports produced empty data cells.** The renderers were called with the human-readable column labels (`Provider`, `Resolved model`) and used those same labels to look up each data cell — but rows are keyed by SQL column names (`provider`, `resolved_model`). Every `row.get(\"Provider\")` returned `None`, so CSV/XLSX exports were a header with nothing beneath. JSON and TXT were unaffected (JSON uses column names; TXT reads by column name). The aggregate (grouped) exports were also unaffected.\n2. **TXT truncated long values** to the header width (`nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b` → `nvidia/nemotro`). Columns now widen to the longest value and never truncate.\n\n**New capability (your request):**\n- **Provider/Model filter** in the export modal — comma-separated, datalist-backed (suggestions from the request stats), OR semantics. `provider=nvidia_nim,novita` exports exactly those two providers. Web Search scope keeps the provider filter and hides the model filter (no models there).\n- **\"All time\" period** — sends no `since`, exports the full lifetime table.\n\n## Verification\n\n- CSV/XLSX data cells now round-trip real values (verified live against a throwaway server + in the browser download path).\n- Multi-provider/model filters return the exact union (1000 rows = 500 nvidia_nim + 500 deepseek; providers/models correct).\n- Websearch hides the model filter; provider filter returns exactly the matching rows.\n- \"All time\" returns the full table (2000 request rows, 300 websearch rows).\n- New tests assert data cells are present (the coverage gap that let the empty-cell bug ship) and multi-value filters work. Each new guard was confirmed to **fail against the pre-fix code**.\n- Local CI: ruff format/check clean, `ty check` clean, 3711 passed / 26 skipped. The 16 failing tests are the documented pre-existing PowerShell installer failures (`FCC release wheel checksum mismatch` — they download a real wheel; identical on unmodified `main`). This diff touches no installer code.\n\n## Files changed\n\n- `core/export.py` — renderers take `columns` (row keys) + `headers` (labels); TXT widens, never truncates.\n- `api/admin_export_routes.py` — pass both to CSV/XLSX.\n- `core/request_log.py`, `websearch/analytics.py` — comma-separated provider/model → IN clauses.\n- `api/admin_static/{index.html,admin.js,admin.css}` — All time period, provider/model filter row.\n- Tests + version 5.3.5 → 5.4.0 (MINOR: new capability).\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- TXT now buffers the exported rows in memory to compute column widths (single-pass generator constraint). For a 50k+ row export of text this is a few MB — acceptable for a \"readable report\"; JSON/CSV/XLSX remain fully streaming.\n- The `include_content=true` param the websearch UI sends is dead (the backend derives it from field selection) — left in place, harmless.\n- Multi-model filter matches `resolved_model OR requested_model` — a row matches if either references the selected model.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
