    "message": "fix(export): CSV/XLSX detail exports wrote empty data cells; add provider/model filter + All time period\n\nThe request-log and web-search detail export renderers passed the human-readable\ncolumn labels to the data-cell lookup, so CSV and XLSX exports produced a header\nrow with every data cell empty (\"exports nothing / a few sloppy rows\"). The\nrenderers now take columns (row keys) and headers (labels) separately: labels\nfor the header row, column names for cell reads. TXT truncated long values\n(model ids, endpoints) to the header width; it now widens columns to the longest\nvalue and never truncates.\n\nNew capability: the export modal gains a provider/model filter (comma-separated,\ndatalist-backed, OR semantics) and an \"All time\" lifetime period. Backend\nprovider/model filters accept comma-separated lists via IN clauses; the websearch\nprovider filter does the same. \"All time\" sends no since/until.\n\nVerified: CSV/XLSX data cells round-trip real values (live server + browser),\nmulti-provider/model filters return the exact union, websearch scope hides the\nmodel filter, \"All time\" returns the full table. Tests assert data cells are\npresent (the gap that let the empty-cell bug ship in 5.2.0) and multi-value\nfilters work; each new guard was confirmed to fail against the pre-fix code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
